# The city footage for "How cities work".
#
# Player commands only (this runs under --record), with the real model writing the prose — no
# --playground. Spawns on the city at vertex 2701 of seed 42 — a port city on the plain, farms and
# orchards around it — via the flags in storyboard.json:
#   --skip-childhood --seed 42 --no-encounters --allow-reentry --start-at city --period dawn
# `clip` names the spans the storyboard cuts; `hold` lets a shot breathe before the next click.
# Timeouts are long: on the CPU the model takes a minute or more per passage. The cutter
# fast-forwards those waits (timeline: model-busy / model-idle).

# The model loads before the menu is offered.
wait mode MainMenu 900
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 60
click continue
wait mode WorldView 300

clip map
hold 3
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 900
hold 0.5
clip end map

clip arrive
advance 12 900
hold 4
cursor rest
hold 2
clip end arrive

regions
clip act
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 900
hold 2
regions
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 900
hold 1
click continue
advance 12 900
hold 4
clip end act

clip next
click button
wait 900
advance 12 900
hold 4
clip end next

# The menu, the way a player opens it: Escape, then the protagonist screen and one of its tabs.
clip menu
pause
wait 30
hold 1.5
elements
click menu Protagonist
wait 30
hold 2
elements
click tab inventory
wait 30
hold 3
click back
wait 30
hold 1
clip end menu
state
quit
